# TwinLight environment — copy to .env (git-ignored) and fill in.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# The twin reads ./.env from its working directory at startup (or the file
# named by --env-file); a variable set in the real environment wins over the
# same name here. `docker compose` reads this same file from the project root
# and passes TWINLIGHT_API_TOKENS to the twin container.
#
# Generate a token with:
#   python -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))'

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Server side: the tokens the twin accepts.
#
# Setting this turns authentication ON for both REST and gNMI: every request
# must carry `Authorization: Bearer <token>` (gRPC: `authorization` metadata),
# except GET /health. Leave it unset or empty and both interfaces stay open,
# with no authentication code running at all.
#
# Comma- or whitespace-separated. Each entry is a bare token or name:token;
# the name is what the logs and GET /internal/whoami report, so you can tell
# clients apart and revoke one without touching the others. At least 16
# characters each, from the RFC 6750 set: letters, digits and -._~+/ (with
# optional trailing =).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWINLIGHT_API_TOKENS=ui:REPLACE-with-a-generated-token,onos:REPLACE-with-another-one

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Client side: the one token twinlight-client and twinlight-soft-failure
# present (examples/demo_services.py reads it from the environment only).
# Must be one of the tokens above. Overridden by their --token flag.
#
# The ONOS integration reads it too: docker-compose.onos.yml passes it to the
# T-API adapter, and the integrations/onos scripts present it to the twin. The
# adapter serves ONOS without credentials, so anyone who can reach its port
# (8282) uses the twin with this token. One token serves the twin's CLIs,
# the scripts and the adapter, so revoking it cuts off all of them, and the
# twin's log cannot tell them apart. See integrations/onos/README.md, section
# Authentication.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# TWINLIGHT_API_TOKEN=REPLACE-with-a-generated-token
